# {{lb|en|US spelling}} A very small [[urban]] [[neighborhood]], usually extending the length of a [[city block]] or smaller.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1982|author=Claude S. Fischer|title=To Dwell Among Friends: Personal Networks in Town and City|publisher=University of Chicago Press|isbn=9780226251387|page=276|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=H6ni9D3_ScAC&pg=PA276&dq=%22microneighborhood%22&hl=&cd=1&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22microneighborhood%22&f=false|text=Occasionally the resultant '''microneighborhood''' was a single block; more often it was part of one block plus the face of the block across the street. Or it might be both sides of a street for several blocks.}}